  "notes": "Reference causal MLA prefill attention over the current token sequence. Workers dynamically claim complete token rows to balance both increasing causal-history cost and asymmetric core throughput. Query/head rows remain independent and retain their original reduction order; planner-owned score rows prevent cross-worker aliasing. The model-derived softmax scale is explicit."
